<p>Bommasandra used to be known mainly for its industrial area and for Narayana Health City on Hosur Road. Since the Yellow Line metro opened in 2025, with its terminus at Delta Electronics Bommasandra and a station at Biocon Hebbagodi, it has also become one of South Bangalore's busiest apartment corridors. New owners here are often first-time buyers working in Electronic City, at the hospital campus or in the factories, and most are fitting out a compact 2 BHK on a careful budget. This guide builds on our <a href="/interior-designers-bangalore/">Bangalore designer guide</a> for homes in Bommasandra, Hebbagodi and the Jigani link road.</p>

