<h2>Designing a compact 2 BHK</h2>
<p>New flats here tend to be efficient rather than generous. Every wall has to earn its place.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Foyer:</strong> a shallow shoe cabinet with a seat and a key drawer stops shoes spreading into the living room. See <a href="/furniture/shoe-rack-design/">shoe rack designs</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Living room:</strong> a wall-hung TV unit with closed storage below and a slim display above, rather than a heavy floor unit. A peripheral false ceiling hides the AC piping.</li>
  <li><strong>Kitchen:</strong> lofts to the ceiling for rarely used vessels, a tall pantry if a wall is free, and drawers in every base unit under the hob.</li>
  <li><strong>Bedrooms:</strong> floor-to-ceiling wardrobes with lofts; sliding doors only where a hinged door would hit the bed. Compare them in <a href="/compare/sliding-vs-hinged-wardrobe/">sliding vs hinged wardrobes</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Utility:</strong> a washer platform with a cabinet above for detergents and a pull-out for the mop and bucket. See <a href="/rooms/utility-area/">utility area design</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Materials for dust, humidity and hard water</h2>
<p>Three local conditions shape the specification: fine dust from the roads and the industrial area, monsoon humidity from June to October, and hard borewell or tanker water.</p>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Condition</th><th>Choose</th><th>Avoid</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Dust</td><td>Closed wall units, gasketed wardrobe doors, matte or textured laminate, groove handles</td><td>Long open shelves, high-gloss shutters that show every speck</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Humidity</td><td>BWP plywood for kitchen base units and vanities, sealed edges, boards stored off the floor</td><td>MDF or particle board near water, unsealed cut edges</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Hard water</td><td>Steel 304 sink and baskets, quartz or sealed dark granite, matte tiles behind the sink, RO point</td><td>Light polished granite, clear glass backsplash, chrome fittings without a filter</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Board grades are explained in <a href="/compare/bwp-vs-bwr-vs-mr-plywood/">BWP vs BWR vs MR plywood</a>, and finishes in the <a href="/materials/laminate-guide/">laminate guide</a>.</p>

<h2>Rental flats near the industrial area</h2>
<p>Many owners in Bommasandra furnish flats to let to professionals and hospital staff. A rental specification should be durable, quick to install and cheap to repair: laminate shutters, BWP plywood under sinks, hinged wardrobes with lofts, granite counters, LED panel lights and branded but mainstream taps. Furnish the basics well and leave loose furniture to tenants unless you are aiming for a fully furnished rent.</p>

<h2>Choosing a firm near Bommasandra</h2>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Find firms that manufacture nearby</strong>Bommasandra, Jigani and Chandapura have many workshops. A local factory shortens delivery and repair times.</li>
  <li><strong>Visit a finished flat</strong>Ideally a compact 2 BHK in a new tower, so you can see how storage was fitted.</li>
  <li><strong>Visit the factory</strong>Check the panel saw, the edge-bander and how boards are stored in the monsoon.</li>
  <li><strong>Compare itemised quotes</strong>Board grade and brand, finish, hardware brand, sizes and GST on separate lines. Our <a href="/planning/how-to-choose-interior-designer/">designer selection guide</a> has a scorecard.</li>
  <li><strong>Agree the timeline in writing</strong>With milestone payments and a warranty.</li>
</ol>

